  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutional and human capacities in STEM in East Asia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This workplan includes one RP and will focus on strengthening STEM capacity including digital literacy and data literacy for girls and women in the cluster countries. In ROK, a new partnership UNESCO-Syensqo-Ewha Womans University will be sought to move forward women scientist&#x2019;s position and increased interest and enrolment of girls in Science through competition and training workshops and in coordination with EDU sector. In Mongolia, activities will focus on women scientist&#x2019;s empowerment and raised visibility with the Mongolian Academy of Sciences and communication with L&#x2019;Oreal will continue for exploring a FWIS in Mongolia.</narrative>
  </description>
